{"name":"Insignia","hex":"#285294","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"insignia","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A patch or other object that indicates a person's official or military rank, or membership in a group or organization.","A symbol or token of personal power, status, or office, or of an official body of government or jurisdiction."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of insignium","plural of insigne"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/insignia"}],"entries":[{"title":"Insignia","blocks":[{"text":"An insignia is a sign or mark distinguishing a group, grade, rank, or function. It can be a symbol of personal power or that of an official group or governing body."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/SP-10_Capitan_General.svg/330px-SP-10_Capitan_General.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insignia","wikidata":"Q552345"},{"title":"Insignia (Xbox)","blocks":[{"text":"Insignia is a free, non-commercial server that has restored the functionality of Xbox Live for the original Xbox. Insignia was created via closed-source reverse engineering of the original Live server software, hosted on Insignia's own servers, and its aim is to support every game that had Xbox Live support. Insignia is currently in public beta. Some games are either not supported yet or are supported on a limited basis."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3d/Insignia_Logo.svg/330px-Insignia_Logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Insignia_(Xbox)","wikidata":"Q124661212"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Roman_Standards.jpg/500px-Roman_Standards.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Roman_Standards.